@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# Asset sources of truth
+
+This directory contains runtime assets. Do not keep backup or copy files next
+to active assets; version control is the history.
+
+## Galaxy data
+
+- `data/star_atlas/star_systems.json` is the single physical star-system catalog.
+- `data/star_atlas/system_details.json` contains detailed celestial definitions.
+- `data/galaxy/real_star_catalog.json` is the background real-star catalog.
+- `data/galaxy/systems.json` is currently a separate legacy political/network
+  dataset consumed by `GalaxyDatabase`; it is not a copy of the physical atlas.
+  It must be migrated deliberately before it can be removed.
+
+## Shared shaders
+
+Reusable shader stages live in `shaders/common/`. Multiple shader programs may
+reference the same stage. Do not duplicate an identical stage into feature
+folders only to give it another filename.
+
+## Generated and historical files
+
+Generated runtime output belongs under `generated/` or `data/celestial/runtime/`.
+Historical versions belong in version control, not in files named `old`, `copy`,
+or `backup`.
